1. Definitions

"Software" means Rainhill: its source code, game data (including the files in
the data/ directory), texts and documentation, in source or compiled form.

"Derivative Work" means any work that contains, is based on, translates,
ports or adapts all or part of the Software, whether modified or not.

"Terminal Application" means a program whose user interface is presented
exclusively as text characters inside a text terminal or console (including
terminal emulators, whether local, remote or running in a web browser), and
which is controlled through that terminal. Auxiliary output that is not a
user interface, such as files, logs or operating-system notifications, does
not change this.

